# The development pack: the disk image muir boots and writes to.
/pack.img

# Compiled output. The Lisp compiler's QFASL files, and the whole of sys/ubin/,
# which the micro assembler writes from sys/ucadr/ --- the microcode from the
# uc-*.lisp files listed in ucadr/ucode.lisp, and the boot PROM from
# ucadr/promh.text.
*.qfasl
/sys/ubin/

# Three exceptions, none of which anything here can make again. The fonts have
# no source form here (docs/fonts.md); demo/tvbgar holds saved arrays rather
# than compiled code; and sys/ucinit records the functions microcompiled into
# the microcode, written once by hand (sys/mlap.lisp, whose writer has no caller).
!/sys/fonts/*.qfasl
!/sys/demo/tvbgar.qfasl
!/sys/sys/ucinit.qfasl

# Output the build writes beside the sources: compiler warning databases, the
# editor's tag tables, and the mail reader's index files.
*cwarns*.lisp
*.tags
*.idx

# The host table, which the SITE system writes from site/hosts.text whenever that
# is newer (:GENERATE-HOST-TABLE, sys/sysdcl.lisp:158-160).
/site/hsttbl.lisp

# COLDRUN is a local build script served to a cold boot, not release source.
/site/coldrun.lisp

# The machine-control tools (tools/: lispm.py over TELNET, console.py over RFB),
# kept here but not yet tracked.
/tools/

# Working notes for Claude Code, and its agents' worktrees: local, not for the
# repository.
/CLAUDE.md
/.claude/

# Local copies of material the repository does not carry, each with a README of
# its own: LM-3's releases in full, to copy from when something turns out to be
# wanted (lm3-99.32/, lm3-100/, lm3-304/), and
# the MIT font sources recovered by the ITS reconstruction project (lmfont/).
# docs/fonts.md has the rest.
/lm3-*/
/lmfont/
